Z||000002||theogre||11-19-2000||01:56 PM||||32 is EGR system flipping out. leaking lines or the rat bag solinoid would be the first things to check.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tom88gt||11-19-2000||08:19 PM||||Check you EGR vacum lines and solenoid wiring first.  Ohm check the solinoid first.  Use "on Line Service Guide".  Check everything else first before you replace the solenoid as they are $$$.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroSTETZ||11-22-2000||12:49 AM||||how do i check said items?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||5
Z||000005||tgowens||11-22-2000||01:48 AM||||check the EGR valve by unplugging the vacuum line leading into it, push your finger up under and into the valve (you will feel a diaphragm which will slowly rise under finger pressure), put your finger over the inlet tube (where you disconnected the vacuum line) and remove your finger from inside the valve - then remove your finger from the vacuum line inlet and you should hear the valve function as air flows through the inlet tube.<P>If the EGR valve functions normally you may have a crack in the EGR tube itself (inspect visually -- usually cracks around the flange) or lastly, the EGR solenoid is bad.<P>------------------<BR>                  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                              <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
